## Glass Card Design

### Hard rule (no exceptions for new/edited UI)

When creating or redesigning **any** card / page surface / table shell / widget container:

1. Use `className="glass-card"` (or `glass-card-frosted` for sheets/dialogs).
2. Place `<div className="glass-card-cap" />` immediately after the opening tag.
3. Do **not** invent a flat white card (`bg-white` + `border-slate-*` + `shadow-sm`) as the main shell.

Forbidden for new card shells:

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — solid white card instead of CAALM glass
<Card className="mb-6 border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
```

Required:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<Card className="glass-card mb-6 overflow-hidden">
  <div className="glass-card-cap" />
  <CardContent className="p-0">{/* or p-4 sm:p-6 */}</CardContent>
</Card>
```

Mockups that show a plain white panel still map to **glass-card** in CAALM — match layout density, not a flat solid fill.

### Card titles (hard rule)

**Every card title carries `sidebar-gradient-text`**: chart cards, table cards, assistant / panel cards, stat cards. No plain slate or black card titles.

- Card title: `h5 sidebar-gradient-text` (16/24, weight 600). Sub-label under it: `caption text-slate-500`.
- Stat-card titles already get the gradient through `MetricStatCard`; do not override it.
- Source of truth for size and weight: the "Cumulative risk averted" card on Risk Averted.

### Glass Card Structure

**ALL cards** must use the glass-card style:

```tsx
<Card className="glass-card">
  <div className="glass-card-cap" />
  <CardContent className="p-4 sm:p-6">
    {/* Content */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

### Glass Card CSS Classes

- **`.glass-card`**: Main container with backdrop blur, white background with opacity, border, and shadow
  - Applied to: `<Card className="glass-card">`
  - Provides: `background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1)`, `backdrop-filter: blur(12px)`, border and shadow effects

- **`.glass-card-cap`**: Decorative cap at the top of the card
  - Applied to: `<div className="glass-card-cap" />` (placed immediately after Card opening tag)
  - Provides: Thin horizontal bar at the top with `background: #d6d7d8` and `opacity: 0.7`

- **`.glass-card-inner`**: Inner content wrapper for nested glass effects
  - Applied to: Nested content areas that need additional blur effect
  - Provides: Enhanced backdrop blur for layered content

### When to Use Glass Cards

**ALWAYS** use glass-card for:
- Dashboard cards and widgets
- Audit log cards
- Stat/metric cards
- Content cards in dialogs
- Widget components (RecentActivity, QuickNotes, WeatherWidget, etc.)
- **Page main content shells** (tables, filter+list panels, task boards, data tables)
- Redesigns of existing pages — replace solid white shells with glass-card

**ALWAYS** include the glass-card-cap div immediately after the Card opening tag

### Stat Cards (Dashboard Pattern)

**CRITICAL**: Stat cards on dashboard pages do **NOT** use `CardHeader`. Content goes directly in `CardContent`:

```tsx
<Card className="glass-card">
  <div className="glass-card-cap" />
  <CardContent className="p-4 sm:p-6">
    <div className="flex items-center justify-between">
      <div>
        <p className="text-sm font-medium sidebar-gradient-text">
          Stat Title
        </p>
        <div className="flex items-center text-3xl font-bold text-slate-700 pt-2">
          <span>Value</span>
          <StatCardIcon className="ml-2" icon={Icon} />
        </div>
        <p className="text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1">Description</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

**Key Rules for Stat Cards:**
- ❌ **NO** `CardHeader` or `CardTitle`
- ❌ **NO** `bg-slate-50` in `CardContent` (only in dialogs)
- ✅ Padding: `p-4 sm:p-6` (responsive)
- ✅ Title: `text-sm font-medium sidebar-gradient-text`
- ✅ Value: `text-3xl font-bold text-slate-700`
- ✅ Icon: `StatCardIcon` mint rounded-square badge (`rounded-xl bg-green/15`)
- ✅ Description: `text-xs text-slate-600 mt-1`

**Reference examples:**
- `src/app/(root)/dashboard/ExecutiveDashboard.tsx` (lines 860-882)
- `src/app/(root)/dashboard/content-creator/ContentCreatorDashboard.tsx` (lines 123-201)

### Stat Cards Grid

**Standard grid layout:**

```tsx
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 mb-6">
  {/* Stat cards */}
</div>
```

- Grid gap: `gap-6` (NOT `gap-4`)
- Responsive: 1 column mobile, 2 columns tablet, 4 columns desktop
- Bottom margin: `mb-6`

### Content Cards

For content cards (like article lists, tables, etc.):

```tsx
<Card className="glass-card">
  <div className="glass-card-cap" />
  <CardContent className="p-4 sm:p-6">
    {/* Content directly here, no CardHeader */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

