## Dialog & Modal Standards

**Hard rule:** Use `ConfirmDialog` (confirms / destructive) or `AppDialog` (forms / multi-step). Do not invent a third chrome. No grey cap bar. Header wash is `bg-[#eefcfe]/60` (default) or `bg-red/5` (destructive) — not indigo `from-blue-50`.

**Widths:** confirm `max-w-[460px]`; form `max-w-[520px]`. Workspace dialogs (document viewer, article editor, adjust plan, HubSpot config, reports) keep their current width via `className`.

**Leave as overlays** (do not convert to AppDialog): `SearchModal`, `DocsSearch`, `FilePreviewDialogImpl`, `LocalPdfPreviewDialog`, `ExpiryAlertModal`, `ContractExpiryModal`.

**Snapshot confirm:** `showCancel={false}` — no Cancel button.

### Confirm / default

```tsx
<ConfirmDialog
  open={open}
  onOpenChange={setOpen}
  icon={<Camera className="h-5 w-5" />}
  title="Run weekly snapshot?"
  description="Save a point-in-time snapshot of the current score."
  facts={[{ label: "Saved to", value: "Snapshot history" }]}
  helperText="You can export any snapshot as a PDF packet later."
  confirmLabel="Save snapshot"
  onConfirm={save}
/>
```

### Form / multi-step

```tsx
<AppDialog
  open={open}
  onOpenChange={setOpen}
  size="form"
  icon={<ShieldCheck className="h-5 w-5" />}
  title="Confirm this change"
  description="Enter the code we emailed you."
  footer={
    <>
      <Button type="button" variant="outline" onClick={() => setOpen(false)}>
        Cancel
      </Button>
      <Button type="button" className="btn-primary" onClick={submit}>
        Save
      </Button>
    </>
  }
>
  {/* fields */}
</AppDialog>
```

### Dialog Requirements

**ALWAYS:**
- Header: full-width wash `bg-[#eefcfe]/60` (default) or `bg-red/5` (destructive); 44px round tinted icon well (teal `bg-[#078FAB]/10` default, `bg-red/10` destructive), title 18px semibold (`text-[#0f5384]` default, `text-red` destructive), one-line description on the same left edge, 40×40 close X
- Body `px-6`; optional facts box (`border-slate-200 bg-slate-50`, label left / value right `text-slate-700`); muted helper; optional orange warning note
- Footer right-aligned `p-6`: outline Cancel, then one committing action
- Confirm uses `btn-primary` (only gradient in the dialog). Destructive uses `.delete-btn` (solid error)
- Pending: spinner + “Saving…” / “Deleting…”, disable buttons and X, block Escape and overlay click
- Error: keep open, inline `role="alert"` above the footer
- Tall content: `max-h-dvh` flex column; body `min-h-0 overflow-y-auto`; header and footer stay visible

**NEVER:**
- Grey top cap (`bg-[#d6d7d8]`)
- Full-width tinted title banner (`from-blue-50 to-indigo-50`, `glass-dialog-wizard-header`)
- Two gradient buttons in one dialog
- `window.confirm` / `confirm()`
- New colors, fonts, radii, shadows, or z-index values

**Reference:** `src/components/ui/app-dialog.tsx`, `src/components/ui/confirm-dialog.tsx`, snapshot confirm on `src/app/(root)/audits/readiness/page.tsx`

