## Dialog and sheet headers

**Hard rule (always):** the icon beside any dialog, alert dialog or sheet title has a **white background** (`bg-white`) with a thin border (`border-[#0f5384]/15`; `border-red/20` for destructive). Never a blue, teal, red or translucent tint. `AppDialog` follows this.

**Back button (always):** when a dialog has a Back button it renders at the top of the dialog, on the same row as the close X (Back left, X right), never in the footer.

**Divider (always):** a divider (`border-b border-slate-200`) follows the dialog title and description.

**Mock-ups:** a provided PNG is a general template, not pixel-perfect; follow its layout and these rules, not exact sizes.

Header layout (Select Contract Type is the reference): optional Back row (Back on the left, the dialog close button on the right), then icon tile (34px, `rounded-[9px]`) + title (17px, bold, `#0f5384`), the description under it (12.5px, slate-500, indented to the title), then a `border-b border-slate-200` divider. No gradient strip behind the header.

