## Dropdown menus (glass, no card-cap)

> **Exception:** inside the IT routes dropdowns are solid white, not glass. See `.cursor/rules/it-routes-dropdowns-and-header.mdc`.

**Hard rule:** Every dropdown / overflow / filter menu uses the **translucent glass panel** (`bg-white/10` + `backdrop-blur` + `border-white/30`). **Never** add a card-cap bar (`glass-card-cap`, `before:h-4` grey strip, or `AppDropdownMenuContent` cap div) to a dropdown.

**Canonical filter / toolbar dropdowns:** Assign Tasks at `/team/tasks` (`TasksFilterBar`). Use the design components below — do not invent one-off Select triggers in filter rows.

| Piece | Use |
|---|---|
| Filter pill select | `CaalmFilterSelect` from `@/components/ui/CaalmFilterSelect` |
| Trigger tokens | `FILTER_PILL_TRIGGER` / `FILTER_DOCK_TRIGGER` from `@/components/ui/filter-pill` |
| Nested people picker | Same glass `DropdownMenu` pattern as `TaskAssigneeFilter` |
| Form fields in dialogs | Radix `Select` is OK; `SelectContent` already uses the shared glass panel |

- Content: `DropdownMenuContent` / `AppDropdownMenuContent` / `DropdownMenuSubContent` from `@/components/ui/dropdown-menu` (shared glass styles, no cap).
- Nested levels (department → division → people) must use the same glass panel — no solid white popovers, no caps.
- **Every** dropdown panel is glass, with no exceptions: Radix `Select` (`SelectContent`), `DropdownMenu*`, `ContextMenu*`, `Menubar*`, and every `SubContent`. Use the shared components as-is. Do **not** pass `bg-*`, `backdrop-blur-*`, `border-slate-*` or `shadow-xl` overrides to a `*Content`, and do not restyle `SelectItem` hover/focus (it already uses `#F2F5F9`). Solid `bg-white/95`, `bg-popover` or `bg-slate-50` dropdown panels are bugs. Only change width, z-index or offsets via `className`.
- Menu row hover / highlight (list items only, not the trigger button): bg `#F2F5F9`, text `#3d5677`, `font-semibold`; default row is `font-normal` with `px-3` horizontal padding. Nested labels use `DROPDOWN_ITEM_LABEL_CLASS`. Do not use `focus:bg-accent`. Hover fill must not go edge-to-edge: keep panel `p-1`, or when the shell is `p-0` (search header), wrap the list in `DropdownScrollArea` with `px-1 py-1`.
- **Scrolling lists:** Wrap scrollable menu / submenu / suggestion list content in `DropdownScrollArea` from `@/components/ui/DropdownScrollArea` (OverlayScrollbars — no native Windows scrollbar arrows). Put `overflow-hidden` on the menu shell; keep horizontal overflow hidden. Submenu chevrons use `mr-[4px]` on shared `DropdownMenuSubTrigger`.

## Overflow menus (3-dot)

**ALWAYS** use the Contracts table trigger (`ActionDropdown`). Do **not** use Lucide `MoreVertical` / `EllipsisVertical` for row or card overflow menus.

```tsx
<DropdownMenu>
  <DropdownMenuTrigger
    className="shad-no-focus rounded-full transition-colors hover:bg-white/30"
    aria-label={`Actions for ${itemName}`}
  >
    <Image src="/assets/icons/dots.svg" alt="" width={34} height={34} />
  </DropdownMenuTrigger>
  <AppDropdownMenuContent align="end">
    <AppDropdownMenuItem icon={Pencil} onClick={...}>
      Edit
    </AppDropdownMenuItem>
    <DropdownMenuSeparator />
    <AppDropdownMenuItem icon={Trash2} tone="danger" onClick={...}>
      Delete
    </AppDropdownMenuItem>
  </AppDropdownMenuContent>
</DropdownMenu>
```

**Required:**
- Icon: `/assets/icons/dots.svg` at `width={34}` `height={34}`
- Trigger: `shad-no-focus rounded-full transition-colors hover:bg-white/30`
- Items: `AppDropdownMenuItem` with a Lucide `icon` (and `tone="danger"` for delete/archive)
- Panel: glass dropdown **without** card-cap
- `aria-label` on the trigger that names the row (`Actions for {title}`)

**Delete / Archive divider (required):** If the menu includes Delete, Archive, or any other destructive item, put `<DropdownMenuSeparator />` immediately **above** that item. Never sit a destructive action flush against Edit / History / other safe actions.

**Reference:** `src/components/ActionDropdown.tsx` (contracts table), `src/components/licenses/LicenseActionDropdown.tsx`

---

## Badges

**ALWAYS** use the CAALM badge pattern from the Contracts table. Do **not** use unstyled shadcn `Badge` variants (`default`, `secondary`, `outline`, `destructive`) as the final look.

```tsx
<span className="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 text-xs rounded-full border bg-green/10 text-green border-green/20">
 Active
</span>```

**Shape (required):** `inline-block px-2 py-0.5 text-xs rounded-full border`

**Status / meaning colors (required):**

| Meaning | Classes |
|---|---|
| Success / active / current | `bg-green/10 text-green border-green/20` |
| Warning / pending / draft | `bg-orange/10 text-orange border-orange/20` |
| Danger / expired / action required | `bg-red/10 text-red border-red/20` |
| Info / category / in progress | `bg-blue/10 text-blue border-blue/20` |
| Neutral / inactive / version | `bg-slate-100 text-slate-600 border-slate-200` |

**Rules:**
- Use custom colors with opacity (`bg-green/10`), never `bg-green-100` / `bg-blue-100`
- Capitalize labels (`Active`, `Draft`), do not dump raw enum strings (`active`)
- `Badge` from `@/components/ui/badge` is allowed only when these classes override the default variant (see department tables). Prefer a `<span>` like `ContractsTableView`

**Reference:** `src/components/ContractsTableView.tsx` (`statusBadge`), `src/components/Card.tsx`, `src/components/licenses/LicenseCard.tsx`

**Status badges:** no colored dots inside the pill; do not truncate label text (`whitespace-nowrap`). If a table cell badge changes, update the matching sheet/detail view to the same component.

---

## Sheet chips (suggestion / selectable pills)

**ALWAYS** use `SHEET_CHIP_IDLE` / `SHEET_CHIP_SELECTED` from `@/components/ui/sheet-chip` for pill-shaped buttons inside assistant and panel sheets — quick prompts, "Ask Next" suggestions, multi-select reason/filter chips. Do not hand-roll the hover classes inline.

```tsx
<button type="button" className={selected ? SHEET_CHIP_SELECTED : SHEET_CHIP_IDLE}>
  {label}
</button>
```

- Idle: `border-slate-200 bg-white/50 text-slate-700`, hover **always** previews the selected look with `hover:border-blue-300 hover:bg-blue-50`
- Selected: solid `#0f5384` fill, white text
- Compose with `cn(SHEET_CHIP_IDLE, "text-left", ...)` for variant needs (alignment, `disabled:` states) — never override the hover colors

**Reference:** `src/components/assistant/CaalmAssistantSheet.tsx` (quick prompts, feedback reason chips), `src/components/audits/ReadinessAiPanel.tsx` (Ask Next)

---

## Data tables

**Hard rule:** Every list / data table in the app must use the **Assign Tasks** chrome as the base template. Domain columns and cells layer on top — do not invent solid white header rows, `bg-slate-50` header bands, or plain `hover:bg-slate-*` body rows.

**Canonical reference:** `/team/tasks` → `src/components/tasks/TasksDataTable.tsx`  
**Design component:** `@/components/ui/caalm-data-table` (styles from `src/lib/ui/data-table-styles.ts`).

| Piece | Use |
|---|---|
| Shell | `CaalmDataTable` (wraps `border-separate border-spacing-0` + `overflow-x-auto pb-4`; applies `DATA_TABLE_INSET` (`px-2 sm:px-4`) itself, so call sites cannot remove the inset) |
| Toolbar above the table (search, filters) | `DATA_TABLE_TOOLBAR_INSET` (`px-4`) so the search field lines up with the table data |
| Header row | `DATA_TABLE_HEADER_ROW` (light grey band) |
| Header cell | `DATA_TABLE_HEADER_CELL` (`text-slate-700`, semibold; + `px-3`; first/last cells use `pl-4` / `pr-4`) |
| Sortable header | `SortableDataTableHead` (`ChevronsUpDown`) — only on columns that sort |
| Body row | `DATA_TABLE_BODY_ROW_CLICKABLE` (or `DATA_TABLE_BODY_ROW_BASE`) |
| Cell padding | `DATA_TABLE_CELL` / `DATA_TABLE_CELL_FIRST` / `DATA_TABLE_CELL_LAST` |
| Empty state | `CaalmDataTableEmpty` |
| Loading | `CaalmDataTableSkeleton` (not a spinner) |
**Also used by:** contracts, licenses, approvals, files, users, roles, audits, settings billing tables.

### Bulk selection, bars and motion

- **Bulk selection:** use `BulkActionDock` (`@/components/ui/bulk-action-dock`): a glass pill fixed 2px above the window bottom and centered on its card, with count badge, actions, and Clear + Esc. Never an in-flow bar that shifts the layout. Selected rows get `bg-blue/10` plus the 2px `#0f5384` left bar.
- **Progress / share bars:** use `AnimatedBar` (`@/components/ui/animated-bar`): grows in once on screen, teal `#078FAB`, track `bg-slate-200`. Do not use the default shadcn `Progress` fill.
- **Page entrance:** blocks reveal on scroll with the shared variants in `@/components/landing/motion` (`softRise`, `fadeUp`, `fadeLeft`, `fadeRight`, `scaleIn`, `staggerContainer`, `viewportOnce`). Wrap cards in a plain `motion.div`; never put the transform on a `glass-card` itself (its CSS transition fights the animation). Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.


When a cell component is shared (status badge, avatar, linked chip), the detail sheet must render the **same** component so table and sheet stay in sync.

