## Dashboard density (anti-clutter)

- One clear primary CTA per section; group secondary actions
- Stat card grids: `gap-6` (not `gap-4`)
- Limit equal-weight card rows to 4 per row on desktop
- Empty/error states: icon + short message (Lucide, not emoji)
- Loading: prefer skeleton components for dense cards; when a spinner is needed, follow **Loading spinners** below

---

## Loading skeletons (hard rule)

A page that loads data shows a skeleton that **mirrors the real layout**: the same grid, the same glass card shells (`glass-card` + `glass-card-cap`, `p-4 sm:p-6`), with inner `Skeleton` lines where the title, values, bars and rows will be. Never one large blank block per section, and never a plain spinner for a page.

- Use `@/components/ui/glass-skeletons`: `GlassCardSkeleton`, `MetricCardSkeleton` (mirrors `MetricStatCard`), `BarRowsSkeleton`, `TableCardSkeleton` (a glass card holding `CaalmDataTableSkeleton`).
- Tables inside cards use `CaalmDataTableSkeleton`.
- Give the skeleton `role="status"` and `aria-busy`, and keep static text (such as a compliance disclaimer) visible instead of blanking it.
- Examples: `ReadinessSkeleton` (Audit Readiness), the loading branch of `RiskAvertedDetailPage`.

## Loading spinners

**Reserved (page loads only):** The branded CAALM spinner — segmented circular arc + teal center mark + optional “Loading…” label — from `LoadingSpinner` in `@/components/ui/loading` at **`size="md"`**, **`size="lg"`**, or **`fullScreen`**. Use only for:

- Initial app / auth gate loads
- Route transitions (`loading.tsx`, Suspense page fallbacks)
- Full-page refresh / first fetch shells when the whole page is waiting

If a **page** load takes time, keep the larger page spinner (`md` / `lg` / `fullScreen`). Do not shrink it to card size on page shells.

**Cards / glass panels (hard rule):** When a `.glass-card`, metric card, widget, or table shell is waiting on data, use a **skeleton** — never a branded `LoadingSpinner` and never a spinning icon.

```tsx
// ✅ Page route loading (branded)
<LoadingSpinner size="md" label="Loading..." />
<LoadingSpinner fullScreen label="Loading..." />

// ✅ List / data table inside a card
<CaalmDataTableSkeleton columns={8} rows={6} />

// ✅ Other cards / widgets
<StatCardSkeleton />
// or Skeleton from @/components/ui/skeleton / LoadingSkeleton

// ❌ Never in a card
<Card className="glass-card">
  <LoadingSpinner size="sm" label="Loading..." />
</Card>
```

**Reference:** `CaalmDataTableSkeleton` in `@/components/ui/caalm-data-table`, `@/components/ui/skeletons`, `src/components/ui/loading.tsx` (page loads only).

