## Consistency Checklist

When creating a new page or component, verify:

- [ ] Page uses standard container: `w-full px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 xl:px-12`
- [ ] Page header uses: `h1 capitalize sidebar-gradient-text`
- [ ] All cards use: `glass-card` class with `glass-card-cap` div
- [ ] Stat cards do NOT use `CardHeader` (content directly in `CardContent`)
- [ ] Stat cards use: `p-4 sm:p-6` padding (NO `bg-slate-50`)
- [ ] Stat cards grid uses: `gap-6` (NOT `gap-4`)
- [ ] Dialogs use professional structure with cap bar, gradient header, and `bg-slate-50` content
- [ ] Custom colors use opacity syntax: `bg-blue/10` (NOT `bg-blue-100`)
- [ ] Icons use brand color: `text-[#0f5384]` for headers
- [ ] Primary buttons use: `btn-primary px-3 sm:px-4` (or `primary-btn`) **with a Lucide icon**
- [ ] Delete buttons use: `delete-btn px-3 sm:px-4` (or `btn-delete`) **with a Lucide icon**
- [ ] All interactive elements have transition effects
- [ ] Text inputs, selects, textareas, and search fields use `border-[0.25px] border-slate-300` (never 1px `border`, white, transparent, or `slate-200` on light fills)
- [ ] Dropdown panels use glass (`DropdownMenuContent` / `AppDropdownMenuContent` / `SelectContent`) with **no card-cap** and **no bg/blur overrides**
- [ ] Scrollable dropdown / submenu lists use `DropdownScrollArea` (not native `overflow-y-auto` scrollbars)
- [ ] Cards / glass panels / tables waiting on data use skeletons (`CaalmDataTableSkeleton` / `StatCardSkeleton` / `Skeleton`) — never branded `LoadingSpinner` or spin icons- [ ] 3-dot overflow menus use `/assets/icons/dots.svg` (34×34) with `shad-no-focus rounded-full hover:bg-white/30` — not Lucide `MoreVertical`
- [ ] Delete / Archive menu items have `<DropdownMenuSeparator />` immediately above them and `tone="danger"`
- [ ] Badges use `inline-block` / `inline-flex` + `px-2 py-0.5 text-xs rounded-full border` plus CAALM status colors — no dots inside; no truncated labels
- [ ] Toolbar / filter-row selects use `CaalmFilterSelect` (Assign Tasks pill standard)
- [ ] Data tables use `CaalmDataTable` / `DATA_TABLE_*` / `CaalmDataTableEmpty` + `SortableDataTableHead` where sorting applies
- [ ] User faces use profile photo when available, else initials via `@/components/ui/avatar`
- [ ] Sheet/detail cells reuse the same badge/avatar/chip components as the table

